+# 9900007 research log
+
+Date: 2026-09-30 UTC. Model: gpt-6-astra, xhigh. Two-hour deadline:07:51 UTC; at most five substantive approaches.
+
+## 05:51–05:54: source and prior-attempt gate
+
+No previous campaign attempt was found for 9900007 in all-state PR searches, branch/path history, or attempt folders. The older 9900005 entry concerns distinct Problem3.1, setwise versus total-variation asymptotic stationarity. Its existence is recorded rather than conflated with this target. The full imported report for 9900007 contains source/literature triage, not a proof.
+
+The indexed primary source pp3–4 defines one-sided processes, product paths and the deterministic synchronous shifts in Problem3.3. Its first question seeks a broad characterization; the following synchronous distance condition is illustrative. Disproving it alone must not be advertised as a full resolution. Its convergence mode is not explicit. Distributional random-shift coupling in the preceding theorem is a different condition. Direct PDF retrieval currently returns502; full-source retrieval and current literature checks continue.
+
+Source-gate completion estimate:60%; target-resolution estimate:0%. No mathematical result is claimed at this checkpoint.
+
+## 05:58–06:02: complete synchronous obstruction, broader target still open in this attempt
+
+The independent-flip process has exact finite-window TV error r/(n+r+1), so its shifted laws converge weakly to a stationary mixture of constant paths. Its finite-history conditional mean decays by the exact factor m(m+1)/(n(n+1)). Conditional-expectation approximation then proves that every coupling with the constant-path limit has mismatch probability tending to1/2, even when the coupled constant depends on the entire original path and extra randomness. The complete product-metric error has limiting law one-half delta0 plus one-half delta1. Fixed finite random offsets, and uniformly tight nonnegative offsets, leave the obstruction intact.
+
+The checker passes885 exact assertions covering42 windows,240 transition products and elementary inequalities. It is a finite diagnostic, not a substitute for the arbitrary-coupling proof. The complete six-page Thorisson finite-window coupling preprint was read; it constructs a sequence of copies and does not remove the single-path consistency issue. Source and prior-art access limitations are preserved.
+
+One substantive construction family used. This resolves only the illustrative coupling proposal. No mechanism for an alternative general two-process characterization was obtained, and ruling out this example cannot rule out every such condition. Stopped the broader search rather than relabeling a partial as a full resolution. Partial-proof completion estimate:100% pending independent review; broader-characterization completion estimate:0%; historical novelty unestablished.
+
+## 06:15: separate scoped review passed
+
+The unchanged frozen partial proof passed an independent adversarial audit, including the arbitrary-coupling conditional projection, infinite limiting arguments, metric changes and dependent finite offsets. All885 author assertions reproduced byte for byte;3,044 independent exact checks passed. The full characterization remains unresolved. Partial-proof and review completion:100%; broader-characterization completion:0%; novelty unestablished. Primary-source access limitations remain explicit.
